WEBVTT

00:00:13.110 --> 00:00:15.660
<i>Huh? Where did all the clouds come from?</i>

00:00:27.420 --> 00:00:29.210
<i>This umbrella...</i>

00:00:29.210 --> 00:00:32.300
<i>Right. I must have borrowed it from Kei.</i>

00:00:32.840 --> 00:00:35.390
<i>I'm sure I went to his place to make curry,</i>

00:00:35.390 --> 00:00:38.550
<i>so why do I have a sports bag with me?</i>

00:00:38.850 --> 00:00:40.100
<i>Well, doesn't matter.</i>

00:00:40.100 --> 00:00:43.560
<i>At least I got to hear that the curry was good.</i>

00:00:47.060 --> 00:00:48.020
<i>It's raining...</i>

00:00:49.020 --> 00:00:52.240
<i>I lost the memories of Ukawa using her ability.</i>

00:00:53.070 --> 00:00:55.700
<i>The whole of Sakurada lost their abilities.</i>

00:00:55.700 --> 00:00:59.780
<i>My mind's being flooded with new memories.</i>

00:01:01.160 --> 00:01:04.500
<i>I see. I can't lose memories,</i>

00:01:04.500 --> 00:01:08.040
<i>so this happens when my memories
are forcibly overwritten.</i>

00:01:08.040 --> 00:01:10.710
<i>My memories of the worlds
with and without abilities</i>

00:01:10.710 --> 00:01:14.170
<i>are colliding with one another.</i>

00:01:14.550 --> 00:01:19.680
<i>Haruki being beside me and Haruki not being here...</i>

00:01:19.680 --> 00:01:23.430
<i>Souma dying and Souma living with us...</i>

00:01:39.780 --> 00:01:43.040
What do you mean by that?

00:01:43.040 --> 00:01:45.620
What are you apologizing for?

00:01:46.370 --> 00:01:47.670
I can't let this message

00:01:48.750 --> 00:01:50.840
be our last one.

00:03:27.060 --> 00:03:28.720
Morning, Kei.

00:03:29.980 --> 00:03:31.890
Morning, Souma.

00:03:36.440 --> 00:03:39.940
What's wrong, Kei? You seem really tired.

00:03:39.940 --> 00:03:42.660
It's nothing. I'm just bad at waking up early.

00:03:42.950 --> 00:03:44.740
I know that.

00:03:44.740 --> 00:03:47.290
But today it seems like it's more than that.

00:03:47.290 --> 00:03:48.290
Why?

00:03:48.290 --> 00:03:51.750
I don't know why, it just seems different.

00:03:52.040 --> 00:03:56.540
You look as tired as if you'd gotten
years older in just one night.

00:03:56.540 --> 00:03:58.670
It's nothing, really.

00:03:58.670 --> 00:03:59.630
I see.

00:04:01.880 --> 00:04:04.140
I made lunch for us today.

00:04:04.140 --> 00:04:05.970
Let's eat it together later.

00:04:05.970 --> 00:04:07.220
Well, see you.

00:04:08.720 --> 00:04:10.350
<i>Amazing.</i>

00:04:10.680 --> 00:04:12.730
<i>Having forgotten about her ability,</i>

00:04:12.730 --> 00:04:15.940
<i>Souma is just an ordinary girl living a happy life.</i>

00:04:16.900 --> 00:04:18.360
How are you feeling?

00:04:18.360 --> 00:04:19.730
I'm fine.

00:04:21.610 --> 00:04:23.990
As far as I can tell, at least.

00:04:23.990 --> 00:04:25.070
I see.

00:04:25.070 --> 00:04:28.200
You really scared me. You'd been feeling well lately.

00:04:29.740 --> 00:04:32.330
Let's get lunch somewhere and go home.

00:04:34.500 --> 00:04:37.000
Your clothes seem a bit loose.

00:04:37.590 --> 00:04:38.670
Have you lost some weight?

00:04:38.670 --> 00:04:40.210
I'm not sure.

00:04:42.300 --> 00:04:44.680
The doctor is apparently examining someone,

00:04:44.680 --> 00:04:47.390
so let's just talk to the nurse and go home.

00:04:50.640 --> 00:04:52.060
I wonder if something happened?

00:04:55.980 --> 00:04:57.060
Let's go.

00:04:59.400 --> 00:05:02.650
Actually, I got a phone call this morning.

00:05:02.650 --> 00:05:04.900
It was your classmate from middle school.

00:05:04.900 --> 00:05:06.240
I see.

00:05:06.240 --> 00:05:07.950
Asai, I think.

00:05:07.950 --> 00:05:09.580
Were you good friends?

00:05:09.580 --> 00:05:10.080
No.

00:05:10.080 --> 00:05:11.620
Really?

00:05:11.620 --> 00:05:13.450
I don't remember him.

00:05:13.450 --> 00:05:15.540
Maybe I'm just forgetting something.

00:05:15.870 --> 00:05:19.210
Anyway, he called about a class reunion.

00:05:19.210 --> 00:05:21.420
He'll be visiting us this evening.

00:05:22.210 --> 00:05:25.170
I wonder what he's like.

00:05:27.180 --> 00:05:28.390
Where do you want to eat?

00:05:28.800 --> 00:05:30.930
Let's go to the roof of the south building.

00:05:30.930 --> 00:05:32.600
It's locked.

00:05:32.600 --> 00:05:33.560
I know.

00:05:33.560 --> 00:05:35.520
We can eat on the stairs there.

00:05:35.520 --> 00:05:38.440
Wouldn't it be really dusty there?

00:05:40.110 --> 00:05:42.230
Do you maybe remember Haruki Misora?

00:05:42.230 --> 00:05:44.900
Haruki? The one from middle school?

00:05:44.900 --> 00:05:45.950
Yeah.

00:05:45.950 --> 00:05:48.530
She was in your class in the first year.

00:05:48.530 --> 00:05:51.200
Well, of course I remember that.

00:05:51.200 --> 00:05:54.040
She fainted and then never came back to school again.

00:05:54.040 --> 00:05:56.960
Rumor has it she had some rare illness.

00:05:56.960 --> 00:05:58.750
It wasn't an illness.

00:05:58.750 --> 00:06:00.590
Did something happen?

00:06:01.630 --> 00:06:04.340
I just remembered her for some reason.

00:06:05.260 --> 00:06:06.760
Say, Souma.

00:06:06.760 --> 00:06:08.720
What do you want to do in the future?

00:06:08.720 --> 00:06:10.300
That's an unexpected topic.

00:06:10.300 --> 00:06:12.560
I was just curious about it.

00:06:12.560 --> 00:06:14.060
It's the same as with Haruki.

00:06:14.430 --> 00:06:16.520
My dreams, huh?

00:06:16.520 --> 00:06:18.560
I used to have a lot.

00:06:18.560 --> 00:06:22.020
In elementary school, I wanted to run a zoo.

00:06:22.020 --> 00:06:23.400
A zoo?

00:06:23.400 --> 00:06:24.900
We went to one on a school trip.

00:06:24.900 --> 00:06:26.780
The penguins were cute, that's why.

00:06:26.780 --> 00:06:27.900
I see.

00:06:27.900 --> 00:06:31.320
There was also a time
I wanted to draw picture books,

00:06:31.320 --> 00:06:34.450
and a time I wanted to become a fashion designer.

00:06:34.450 --> 00:06:35.410
And now?

00:06:35.410 --> 00:06:36.870
I wonder.

00:06:36.870 --> 00:06:38.960
Get into a good enough university,

00:06:38.960 --> 00:06:41.670
and find a job I could do, I guess.

00:06:42.130 --> 00:06:45.420
I realized it doesn't matter what job you have.

00:06:45.420 --> 00:06:48.050
I feel like you can somewhat enjoy anything

00:06:48.050 --> 00:06:51.050
as long as you try to do your best.

00:06:52.350 --> 00:06:53.930
Brings back memories.

00:06:53.930 --> 00:06:57.140
We used to hang out here back in middle school.

00:06:58.180 --> 00:06:58.980
Yeah.

00:07:00.480 --> 00:07:02.730
There's something off about you today.

00:07:02.730 --> 00:07:03.650
Really?

00:07:03.650 --> 00:07:06.650
Yeah. You keep asking questions
you normally wouldn't ask.

00:07:07.030 --> 00:07:09.570
I just wanted to learn more about you.

00:07:09.570 --> 00:07:13.620
I gave up any dreams I had
because I met you, you know.

00:07:13.910 --> 00:07:14.910
Huh?

00:07:14.910 --> 00:07:18.370
Back in elementary school,
knitting was very popular.

00:07:18.910 --> 00:07:20.410
Knitting? Like scarfs?

00:07:20.410 --> 00:07:22.380
Or making plushies, yeah.

00:07:22.380 --> 00:07:26.000
I couldn't understand what
was fun about it, though.

00:07:26.710 --> 00:07:30.760
I thought it just seemed tedious and unpleasant.

00:07:31.340 --> 00:07:33.720
That's also why I didn't really like school.

00:07:34.140 --> 00:07:36.180
Because it's the same thing every day?

00:07:36.180 --> 00:07:39.230
Exactly. Every morning,
you wear the same uniform,

00:07:39.230 --> 00:07:42.400
take the same path,
and go to the same school.

00:07:42.400 --> 00:07:45.940
I felt like I was getting crushed.

00:07:46.440 --> 00:07:51.490
So I wanted my everyday life as an adult
to be more free, released from that.

00:07:52.410 --> 00:07:55.240
But then I met you and realized something.

00:07:55.240 --> 00:07:57.950
Those things actually don't really matter.

00:07:58.870 --> 00:08:03.420
If I go to school and you're there,
I don't mind every day being the same.

00:08:03.420 --> 00:08:05.250
I'd actually prefer if they were.

00:08:05.880 --> 00:08:10.460
If it's for you,
I'm sure I'd enjoy even knitting a sweater.

00:08:12.010 --> 00:08:15.260
Your notebooks today were all new.

00:08:15.260 --> 00:08:17.010
Yeah... What's the matter?

00:08:17.010 --> 00:08:20.810
It almost feels like a new world started today.

00:08:23.390 --> 00:08:27.820
Let's assume that all of our memories are fake.

00:08:27.820 --> 00:08:31.860
You mean like the five minutes hypothesis?

00:08:31.860 --> 00:08:32.530
Yeah.

00:08:32.820 --> 00:08:34.570
It's a thought experiment.

00:08:34.570 --> 00:08:37.950
You can't know that the world
wasn't created five minutes ago.

00:08:37.950 --> 00:08:41.290
All our memories from before that could be fake,

00:08:41.290 --> 00:08:43.040
and the moment the world was created,

00:08:43.040 --> 00:08:47.330
they were planted in our heads
to make us believe it existed before that.

00:08:47.840 --> 00:08:48.540
Assuming so,

00:08:48.880 --> 00:08:53.010
there's no way to know if there was
a different world before this one was created.

00:08:53.010 --> 00:08:57.720
Maybe we had completely different memories
and were doing different things.

00:08:57.720 --> 00:09:01.720
But our memories got rewritten,
and so this world was created.

00:09:02.060 --> 00:09:02.810
Yeah.

00:09:03.600 --> 00:09:06.480
<i>It's not just a thought experiment
anymore. It's reality.</i>

00:09:06.940 --> 00:09:10.650
<i>The world wasn't changed
five minutes ago, but last night.</i>

00:09:11.280 --> 00:09:15.240
<i>What was changed is the memories
of all people living in Sakurada.</i>

00:09:16.570 --> 00:09:20.740
Let's assume that all of our memories are fake.

00:09:21.490 --> 00:09:24.750
Would we still be able to be here together like this?

00:09:25.040 --> 00:09:26.420
Of course.

00:09:26.420 --> 00:09:29.460
Memory isn't reliable to begin with.

00:09:29.920 --> 00:09:32.340
As time passes, our memories get blurry,

00:09:32.340 --> 00:09:35.050
and sometimes we're mistaken from the beginning.

00:09:35.050 --> 00:09:38.220
Still, feelings are born from those very memories.

00:09:38.680 --> 00:09:41.680
Even if we make mistakes,
even if we get the wrong idea,

00:09:41.680 --> 00:09:48.190
the result is the same—I'm here, and so are you—
and I think just believing in that is fine.

00:09:48.190 --> 00:09:50.690
<i>That might make sense without any old memories.</i>

00:09:51.400 --> 00:09:53.650
<i>But I remember everything.</i>

00:09:53.650 --> 00:09:55.650
<i>That's why for me, you're Souma Sumire,</i>

00:09:55.650 --> 00:09:58.360
<i>but not the Souma Sumire I'm used to knowing.</i>

00:09:59.570 --> 00:10:02.660
I got a present from a certain girl.

00:10:02.660 --> 00:10:05.250
She gave it to me in an absurdly roundabout way,

00:10:05.250 --> 00:10:08.080
and put far more effort into making a perfect gift

00:10:08.080 --> 00:10:11.090
than even something like a handmade sweater.

00:10:11.090 --> 00:10:13.250
Good for you. And?

00:10:13.250 --> 00:10:15.590
It's just like you're saying.

00:10:15.590 --> 00:10:19.510
It doesn't matter if we make
mistakes or get the wrong idea.

00:10:19.510 --> 00:10:22.350
My feelings are born from my memories.

00:10:22.350 --> 00:10:23.260
So...

00:10:23.640 --> 00:10:24.350
So?

00:10:24.850 --> 00:10:26.890
I like this world.

00:10:27.390 --> 00:10:31.730
You're laughing, and all kinds
of problems disappear without a trace.

00:10:32.270 --> 00:10:35.860
It might just be the perfect answer.

00:10:36.690 --> 00:10:39.860
But I have my memories.

00:10:40.360 --> 00:10:42.830
That's why I can't stay here forever.

00:10:43.200 --> 00:10:46.250
I don't really get what you're saying.

00:10:46.620 --> 00:10:48.500
I know, I'm sorry.

00:10:48.500 --> 00:10:51.630
I wish I could explain it better.

00:10:51.630 --> 00:10:52.590
But I guess...

00:10:54.250 --> 00:10:57.550
I guess it simply means that I was rejected?

00:11:23.740 --> 00:11:25.740
<i>The town where I was born and raised...</i>

00:11:26.740 --> 00:11:31.420
<i>I lived in this town until my
sixth year of elementary school.</i>

00:11:31.420 --> 00:11:33.500
<i>Nobody here remembers that.</i>

00:11:34.130 --> 00:11:38.210
<i>According to the memories created
yesterday to get rid of inconsistencies,</i>

00:11:38.210 --> 00:11:42.510
<i>I was born in Sakurada,
lost my parents in an accident four years ago,</i>

00:11:42.510 --> 00:11:44.640
<i>and was taken in by the Nakano family.</i>

00:11:48.680 --> 00:11:50.180
<i>The apartment I used to live in...</i>

00:11:51.140 --> 00:11:54.310
<i>I remember the taste of the chicken
curry my mom used to make.</i>

00:11:54.940 --> 00:11:58.190
<i>It was similar to what Souma Sumire
made for me yesterday.</i>

00:11:58.940 --> 00:12:02.700
<i>But my mother's curry
was somehow slightly different.</i>

00:12:08.080 --> 00:12:09.080
Megumi!

00:12:12.250 --> 00:12:13.500
Thank you.

00:12:13.500 --> 00:12:15.710
She always runs off as soon
as I take my eyes off her.

00:12:16.040 --> 00:12:18.750
Is her name Megumi?

00:12:18.750 --> 00:12:19.420
Yes.

00:12:19.880 --> 00:12:21.970
Is it "megumi" as in "blessing"?

00:12:21.970 --> 00:12:22.630
That's right.

00:12:22.630 --> 00:12:26.930
I'm surprised. That's also what my name means.

00:12:26.930 --> 00:12:28.970
They both come from the same character.

00:12:28.970 --> 00:12:30.560
What a coincidence.

00:12:30.560 --> 00:12:33.810
I'd have named her Kei if she'd been born a boy.

00:12:33.810 --> 00:12:35.770
I decided on that a long time ago.

00:12:35.770 --> 00:12:38.400
Based on the same meaning, a boy would be Kei,

00:12:38.400 --> 00:12:39.730
and a girl would be Megumi.

00:12:40.280 --> 00:12:42.490
Why did you choose that name?

00:12:42.490 --> 00:12:43.820
Huh?

00:12:43.820 --> 00:12:48.870
Maybe my parents had the same reason
to name me that, so I'm curious.

00:12:50.200 --> 00:12:52.160
Since it means "blessing",

00:12:52.160 --> 00:12:54.830
there's a lot of love in this name.

00:12:54.830 --> 00:12:56.290
Being blessed means being loved.

00:12:56.580 --> 00:13:00.420
So you wanted her to grow up
with a lot of love in her heart?

00:13:02.170 --> 00:13:05.930
That too, but you call people
by their names all the time, right?

00:13:06.590 --> 00:13:09.640
For example, every time I say her name,

00:13:09.640 --> 00:13:11.930
I say it with a lot of love.

00:13:12.310 --> 00:13:16.060
Her friends as well,
and her future boyfriend, everyone...

00:13:16.060 --> 00:13:18.940
I thought that'd be such a happy thing.

00:13:20.900 --> 00:13:21.940
What's wrong?

00:13:23.110 --> 00:13:25.110
You look as if you're about to cry.

00:13:26.160 --> 00:13:29.780
I did something terrible to my mother and father.

00:13:30.450 --> 00:13:33.330
I betrayed them both in a really cruel way.

00:13:33.620 --> 00:13:36.080
I see. Have you apologized?

00:13:36.080 --> 00:13:38.710
No. I can't.

00:13:38.710 --> 00:13:39.540
Why?

00:13:39.960 --> 00:13:42.800
I don't think I have the right to anymore.

00:13:42.800 --> 00:13:44.300
That's impossible.

00:13:45.760 --> 00:13:50.220
They are your parents and you are their child,
no matter how they feel about it.

00:13:50.220 --> 00:13:52.810
Nothing can ever take that away from you.

00:13:52.810 --> 00:13:55.270
Don't worry about it and go apologize to them.

00:13:55.270 --> 00:13:57.350
Will I be forgiven if I do?

00:13:57.350 --> 00:13:59.060
I wonder.

00:13:59.060 --> 00:14:03.110
Even if you're not, I'm sure they still love you.

00:14:04.650 --> 00:14:05.440
Can I...

00:14:06.110 --> 00:14:07.990
practice my apology?

00:14:08.280 --> 00:14:09.530
Practice?

00:14:09.530 --> 00:14:10.530
Yes.

00:14:10.530 --> 00:14:13.200
I might not be able to do it properly if I don't.

00:14:14.120 --> 00:14:15.000
Sure.

00:14:20.250 --> 00:14:23.000
Mom, I'm sorry.

00:14:25.010 --> 00:14:26.630
I'm really sorry.

00:14:31.180 --> 00:14:32.390
Well done.

00:14:43.980 --> 00:14:45.940
Thank you so much.

00:14:45.940 --> 00:14:47.900
I feel like a weight has lifted from my mind.

00:14:48.280 --> 00:14:50.910
Make sure you apologize to your parents.

00:14:52.320 --> 00:14:53.700
I'll be going then.

00:14:55.240 --> 00:14:56.910
Bye-bye, Kei!

00:14:59.710 --> 00:15:02.130
Goodbye, Megumi.

00:15:29.280 --> 00:15:30.030
Come in.

00:15:33.820 --> 00:15:35.530
Hi. It's been a while.

00:15:35.910 --> 00:15:39.040
I'm sorry, I don't remember you.

00:15:39.450 --> 00:15:41.330
Yeah, I know.

00:15:41.330 --> 00:15:42.960
I'm Asai Kei.

00:15:42.960 --> 00:15:45.170
I met you in April two years ago.

00:15:45.710 --> 00:15:47.960
Do you remember Souma Sumire?

00:15:47.960 --> 00:15:49.800
She's our mutual acquaintance.

00:15:50.170 --> 00:15:52.930
We've talked a lot.

00:15:52.930 --> 00:15:56.180
A whole season would come and go
before I could explain it all.

00:15:56.600 --> 00:15:58.640
We really have talked a lot.

00:15:59.890 --> 00:16:02.060
I want you to remember all that.

00:16:02.060 --> 00:16:04.980
I don't feel the need to.

00:16:04.980 --> 00:16:07.480
I want you to remember it for me.

00:16:07.480 --> 00:16:08.940
I couldn't, even if I tried.

00:16:09.280 --> 00:16:10.190
There's a way.

00:16:14.160 --> 00:16:17.370
A certain girl threw absolutely everything away

00:16:17.370 --> 00:16:19.200
and gave me a present.

00:16:20.700 --> 00:16:24.330
With this picture, we can bring back your memories.

00:16:24.790 --> 00:16:27.090
I don't think that's possible.

00:16:27.420 --> 00:16:28.960
But it is.

00:16:28.960 --> 00:16:32.930
There's a place I want to take you to
for you to remember everything.

00:16:36.350 --> 00:16:40.100
Two months ago, I talked to you at that bus stop we were just at.

00:16:40.470 --> 00:16:42.730
I got a message from you.

00:16:42.730 --> 00:16:43.350
A message?

00:16:44.230 --> 00:16:45.100
This.

00:16:45.940 --> 00:16:48.070
Did I send this?

00:16:48.520 --> 00:16:51.860
If I reply to it, you'll get a message.

00:16:54.070 --> 00:16:54.950
I did.

00:16:55.360 --> 00:16:59.450
This proves that you sent
the message I just showed you.

00:16:59.740 --> 00:17:01.450
That's not quite right.

00:17:01.950 --> 00:17:03.910
More accurately,

00:17:03.910 --> 00:17:07.540
it proved that it was sent from your address.

00:17:07.540 --> 00:17:08.380
Yes.

00:17:08.380 --> 00:17:12.210
For now, I'll accept the fact that
you and I were acquaintances.

00:17:12.670 --> 00:17:16.470
Why are you trying to bring back my memories?

00:17:17.010 --> 00:17:21.470
We made a promise to eat dinner together.

00:17:21.470 --> 00:17:23.980
I'd like you to remember that promise, if possible.

00:17:34.190 --> 00:17:37.280
<i>What did I do wrong?</i>

00:17:37.280 --> 00:17:40.990
<i>I only wanted to be with Kei.</i>

00:17:43.040 --> 00:17:45.000
The person who lived here

00:17:45.000 --> 00:17:47.750
moved out of Sakurada this summer.

00:17:47.750 --> 00:17:49.330
It's an empty house now.

00:17:50.840 --> 00:17:53.300
Grasp one edge of the picture and don't release it.

00:17:53.670 --> 00:17:54.970
I understand.

00:17:56.010 --> 00:17:59.180
You might be startled by what will happen now,

00:17:59.180 --> 00:18:00.930
but try to stay calm.

00:18:00.930 --> 00:18:02.220
I'll try.

00:18:03.270 --> 00:18:04.730
Okay, let's do this.

00:18:13.650 --> 00:18:15.070
Remember, Haruki.

00:18:15.440 --> 00:18:17.450
What just happened?

00:18:18.070 --> 00:18:20.280
My memories are all mixed up.

00:18:20.280 --> 00:18:23.410
Don't worry about it, just accept them all.

00:18:23.410 --> 00:18:25.410
There are abilities in this town.

00:18:25.410 --> 00:18:27.160
You have the power to reset.

00:18:27.160 --> 00:18:29.290
I know that.

00:18:29.290 --> 00:18:31.590
But I haven't left Sakurada.

00:18:32.130 --> 00:18:33.800
Why did I forget?

00:18:33.800 --> 00:18:36.760
Because abilities disappeared from Sakurada.

00:18:36.760 --> 00:18:40.010
In this place, you can remember them, though.

00:18:40.390 --> 00:18:41.640
Asai Kei.

00:18:41.640 --> 00:18:43.680
What is it that you know?

00:18:44.010 --> 00:18:46.930
We're currently in Sakurada from
the time before abilities disappeared.

00:18:46.930 --> 00:18:48.690
To be exact, its replica.

00:18:49.350 --> 00:18:51.360
I was always by your side.

00:18:51.860 --> 00:18:53.440
I have all the memories you've lost.

00:18:54.070 --> 00:18:55.530
I can't remember.

00:18:56.030 --> 00:18:58.280
I can't remember you.

00:18:58.820 --> 00:18:59.490
Yeah,

00:19:00.070 --> 00:19:01.370
I know.

00:19:01.370 --> 00:19:03.280
Abilities are absolute.

00:19:03.280 --> 00:19:06.040
It's not something you can
overcome with love or friendship.

00:19:06.040 --> 00:19:07.790
Then how...

00:19:07.790 --> 00:19:09.370
Use your reset.

00:19:10.210 --> 00:19:11.670
I can't.

00:19:11.670 --> 00:19:14.460
I remembered how to use it,

00:19:14.460 --> 00:19:16.920
but I don't believe now is the right time to use it.

00:19:17.260 --> 00:19:19.670
I want you to trust me. Haruki.

00:19:21.300 --> 00:19:23.680
I don't have any reason to trust you.

00:19:25.060 --> 00:19:26.600
Today,

00:19:26.600 --> 00:19:29.560
I met Souma Sumire in the place
I always spent time with you.

00:19:30.440 --> 00:19:32.480
I talked to her,

00:19:32.480 --> 00:19:35.440
and experienced exactly
what I'm now trying to erase.

00:19:36.400 --> 00:19:38.690
I saw my hometown for the first time in four years.

00:19:39.150 --> 00:19:42.450
I saw the home I can never return to again.

00:19:42.740 --> 00:19:46.790
I met my mother again,
learned that I had a little sister,

00:19:46.790 --> 00:19:48.370
and learned the story behind my name.

00:19:51.920 --> 00:19:53.580
I'm sure I'm a coward.

00:19:54.540 --> 00:19:57.380
I've never been able to show my feelings.

00:19:58.130 --> 00:20:00.380
I've been scared of showing my weaknesses.

00:20:01.470 --> 00:20:04.590
Even in front of Souma, even in my hometown,

00:20:04.590 --> 00:20:07.260
even reuniting with my mother, I was unable to cry.

00:20:08.270 --> 00:20:09.310
But I...

00:20:10.100 --> 00:20:13.900
If it's possible,
I want to fix all kinds of mistakes I made.

00:20:15.310 --> 00:20:19.650
<i>When I come across someone crying,
I use my reset ability.</i>

00:20:21.400 --> 00:20:23.910
Haruki... It's time to reset!

00:20:25.820 --> 00:20:26.530
Reset.

00:20:36.540 --> 00:20:38.040
Save.

00:20:39.550 --> 00:20:42.420
Seems like we've reset.

00:20:47.760 --> 00:20:49.560
Did something happen?

00:20:49.890 --> 00:20:52.350
Yeah, a lot.

00:20:53.270 --> 00:20:55.440
A lot happened, really.

00:20:57.440 --> 00:20:58.570
My heart aches.

00:21:03.900 --> 00:21:05.410
Are you okay?

00:21:10.490 --> 00:21:12.370
If we don't do anything, in two days,

00:21:12.370 --> 00:21:14.460
abilities will disappear from Sakurada.

00:21:15.790 --> 00:21:17.670
Is such a thing possible?

00:21:17.960 --> 00:21:20.550
We reset because I didn't want it to be like that.

00:21:20.550 --> 00:21:23.970
Abilities are a necessity in Sakurada, aren't they?

00:21:23.970 --> 00:21:25.800
They aren't necessary.

00:21:25.800 --> 00:21:27.720
It's not like they have to exist.

00:21:28.050 --> 00:21:31.180
But I like them.

00:21:31.180 --> 00:21:34.600
I like how people acquire them
by wishing for something.

00:21:34.940 --> 00:21:36.850
Like?

00:21:38.310 --> 00:21:41.110
Haruki, I made a decision.

00:21:41.110 --> 00:21:42.860
I'll rule over all abilities in Sakurada.

00:21:43.650 --> 00:21:45.320
Rule?

00:21:45.860 --> 00:21:46.820
Yeah.

00:21:48.240 --> 00:21:50.580
The person who has the MacGuffin

00:21:50.580 --> 00:21:53.450
can rule over all the abilities in Sakurada.

00:21:54.910 --> 00:21:56.410
Next Episode

00:21:56.410 --> 00:21:58.540
Seems like I'm overlooking something.

00:21:58.540 --> 00:21:59.630
I told you not to come near me.

00:21:59.630 --> 00:22:02.000
Don't you go pushing all the sadness
onto me and disappearing like that.

00:22:02.000 --> 00:22:03.130
How unpleasant.
Don't you go pushing all the sadness
onto me and disappearing like that.

00:22:03.130 --> 00:22:04.380
Will it be possible to save Souma Sumire?

00:22:04.380 --> 00:22:05.340
I don't want to create a girl
whose only purpose is to disappear.
Will it be possible to save Souma Sumire?

00:22:05.340 --> 00:22:05.920
I don't want to create a girl
whose only purpose is to disappear.

00:22:05.920 --> 00:22:08.180
Kei, use the clairvoyance ability.
I don't want to create a girl
whose only purpose is to disappear.

00:22:08.180 --> 00:22:09.930
Kei, use the clairvoyance ability.

00:22:16.350 --> 00:22:20.310
On such a cold dark sky of grey

00:22:22.610 --> 00:22:26.530
Rises the sun, which breathes life into it

00:22:28.610 --> 00:22:32.780
A scenery so plain and so mundane

00:22:33.080 --> 00:22:42.380
And yet it seems to break my heart, it's so dear to me

00:22:43.250 --> 00:22:46.840
As the time never stops passing by

00:22:46.840 --> 00:22:49.220
You get lost while searching for

00:22:49.220 --> 00:22:53.100
Pure like the rays of a morning star

00:22:53.100 --> 00:22:56.020
What we all yearn for the most

00:22:56.020 --> 00:22:59.440
In what colors bliss is dyed

00:22:59.560 --> 00:23:02.060
Struggling against all your past mistakes

00:23:02.060 --> 00:23:05.110
At last from the answer you found kindness fills your heart

00:23:05.690 --> 00:23:08.280
More beautiful than anything you know

00:23:08.280 --> 00:23:11.910
And you find it behind a dark veil of sadness

00:23:11.910 --> 00:23:14.410
If I closed my eyes and stopped my thoughts

00:23:14.410 --> 00:23:16.160
If it were so simple to just

00:23:16.160 --> 00:23:19.160
Lock your own heart

00:23:19.160 --> 00:23:22.290
How lovely life would be

00:23:22.290 --> 00:23:27.550
But I believe you have the key

00:23:28.340 --> 00:23:33.890
To let my soul be free
